# scenarios/9_accruals.books: loaded by ledger_server into 9_accruals.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	9. The year end: costs in the year they belong to
about	A cost belongs to the year it is used in, not the year it is paid. Rent for a year paid on 1 October is three months of this year and nine of the next: at the year end the nine go to Prepaid expenses, an asset (charges à reporter, over te dragen kosten).
about	The other way round, December's electricity is used this year but billed in January: it is a cost now, owed under Accrued expenses, a liability (charges à imputer, toe te rekenen kosten). Both are undone at the start of the next year.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	490000	asset	Prepaid expenses
account	492000	liability	Accrued expenses
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	610000	expense	Rent
account	612000	expense	Energy
